From: Serj Targarien <xergy10@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: give the RGB20SX a linear backlight scale

Without brightness-levels the pwm-backlight driver builds a CIE 1931 curve
(1666 steps on this board), so frontends that map their own levels onto a
linear scale come out far too dark. ROCKNIX's RGB20SX device tree uses a
linear 0-255 table with 77 as the default; this matches it.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-powkiddy-rgb20sx.dts	2026-11-05 20:50:19.154173420 +0100
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-powkiddy-rgb20sx.dts	2026-11-05 20:50:19.156424304 +0100
@@ -96,3 +96,14 @@
 	/delete-property/ sd-uhs-sdr104;
 	sd-uhs-sdr50;
 };
+
+/*
+ * slotsq: a linear 0-255 backlight scale, as ROCKNIX's RGB20SX device tree has. Without a
+ * table the kernel builds its own perceptual curve (1666 steps), and slot's brightness
+ * levels, which apply their own curve for a linear scale, come out far too dark.
+ */
+&backlight {
+	brightness-levels = <0 255>;
+	num-interpolated-steps = <255>;
+	default-brightness-level = <77>;
+};
